note qty_shamt: shl and shr of integer values by a qty amount (omc type 13, a u64). omc admits a shift whose
note amount has another integer type and tests the amount's register against the value's width (bo_schk,
note trap 7). The operands are parameters, so nothing folds. A wrong value returns its own code 1..5; the
note last shift, a uint by 32 (its width), traps 7 (exit 107).
fn q1 a ulong s qty to ulong
ret shl a s
end
fn q2 a uint s qty to uint
ret shr a s
end
fn q3 a long s qty to long
ret shr a s
end
fn q4 a uchar s qty to uchar
ret shl a s
end
fn q5 a short s qty to short
ret shl a s
end
fn main to int
if ne q1 1 qty 63 9223372036854775808
ret 1
end
if ne q2 4294967295 qty 4 268435455
ret 2
end
if ne q3 4096 qty 5 128
ret 3
end
if ne q4 1 qty 7 128
ret 4
end
if ne q5 3 qty 4 48
ret 5
end
x = q2 1 qty 32
ret int and x 255
end
